Subject: Request for Provisioning Three New Disks on UAT Database Server

Dear Infra Team,

We would like to request the provisioning of three new disks on the UAT database server to address persistent performance issues. Below is the detailed justification for this request:

The Application team has been observing database slowness for the past few months, which is adversely impacting our SLA commitments for timely feed deliveries.

Based on our investigation, the Cloud team recommended enabling PvSCSI on the database server for improved I/O performance. However, we encountered a limitation.

Enabling PvSCSI failed due to the server running Windows Server 2016, which does not support PvSCSI.

Additionally, the Cloud team has confirmed that existing disks cannot be shrunk, and to enhance performance on the current LSI controller, disks of optimal size are required.

As an alternate solution, we propose provisioning three new disks, migrating the databases to them, and subsequently decommissioning the existing disks. This approach is expected to significantly improve database performance.

We request your support in provisioning these disks at the earliest possible to help us mitigate the performance bottleneck and meet our SLA commitments.

Please let us know if any further details are required.
